-- ===========================================================================
-- TESTS FROM THE SOURCE.
--
-- Every expected value below was worked out from the text of s 66 (lines
-- 2454-2484) before the rule it exercises was run, and the working is in the
-- comment beside it.  Where a test rests on one reading of a fork, the fork is
-- named (F1 ... in NOTES.md).  The amounts are invented scenario inputs, in
-- shekels; none is a figure of the law.  A failing assertion is a finding:
-- the expected values are not to be edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 66(d), the common source`

`no common source` MEANS NOTHING

-- (a), (b) both limbs, not at home: all three conditions hold.
`a common source meeting (a), (b), not at home` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)
-- (a) fails: one spouse's exertion is not required.
`a common source failing (a)` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` FALSE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)
-- (b) fails on its first limb, then on its second.
`a common source failing (b), matching` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` FALSE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)
`a common source failing (b), proportion` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` FALSE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)
-- (c): at home, both requirements met; then each missing.
`a common source at home meeting (c)` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` TRUE `; most activity at home` TRUE)
`a common source at home, not permanent` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` TRUE)
`a common source at home, most activity elsewhere` MEANS
    JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` TRUE `; most activity at home` FALSE)

GIVEN `source` IS A MAYBE `A common source of income`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `source` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` EMPTY `; common source` `source`

-- (d)(1): spouses with no common source are not within (d) at all.
#ASSERT     `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `no common source`)
-- (d)(1)(a)-(c) all met.
#ASSERT     `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source meeting (a), (b), not at home`)
#ASSERT     `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source at home meeting (c)`)
-- "רק אם התקיימו כל אלה": each one failing shuts (a).
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source failing (a)`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source failing (b), matching`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source failing (b), proportion`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source at home, not permanent`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(d) — subsection (a) applies to` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source at home, most activity elsewhere`)
-- (d) shuts (a)(1) itself (fork F1, the couple reading): the woman may not claim.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source failing (a)`)
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`two salaried spouses in 2025, the woman claiming, with common source` `a common source meeting (a), (b), not at home`)

§ `Tests — section 66(a)(1), what may be calculated separately`

-- The five pensions of the s 1 definition, paras (1)-(4) and (3A).
#ASSERT     `a pension` `a pension paid by a former employer`
#ASSERT     `a pension` `a pension from a pension provident fund`
#ASSERT     `a pension` `a pension paid to the survivors of a person within paragraph (1) or (2)`
#ASSERT     `a pension` `a pension for loss of working capacity`
#ASSERT     `a pension` `a taxable pension paid by the National Insurance Institute`
-- Not pensions: business, employment, (5) a grant, (6) a commuted sum (fork F2), (7) rent.
#ASSERT NOT `a pension` `from a business or profession`
#ASSERT NOT `a pension` `from employment`
#ASSERT NOT `a pension` `a grant received on retirement or on death`
#ASSERT NOT `a pension` `a sum received on the commutation of a pension within paragraphs (1) to (4)`
#ASSERT NOT `a pension` `rent from an asset used for ten years to produce income from personal exertion`

-- The proviso: a pension with neither condition stays out; either condition lets it in.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` (`income of kind` `a pension paid by a former employer` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` (`income of kind` `a pension paid by a former employer` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` TRUE  `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` (`income of kind` `a pension from a pension provident fund` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` TRUE)
-- Not a pension, so the proviso does not reach it, whatever the two facts.
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` (`income of kind` `from a business or profession` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` (`income of kind` `a sum received on the commutation of a pension within paragraphs (1) to (4)` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)

-- A spouse with a salary of 60,000 and a former employer's pension of 20,000
-- that meets neither condition: 60,000 may be calculated separately; 20,000
-- may not; 80,000 is her whole income from personal exertion.
`a woman with a salary and a pension that does not qualify` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion`
        (LIST `a salary of` 60000, `income of kind` `a pension paid by a former employer` `of` 20000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
        `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of` `a woman with a salary and a pension that does not qualify` EQUALS 60000
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may not be calculated separately, of` `a woman with a salary and a pension that does not qualify` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the taxable income from personal exertion of` `a woman with a salary and a pension that does not qualify` EQUALS 80000

-- A spouse whose only income from personal exertion is that pension has
-- nothing (a)(1) can calculate separately, so no claim lies.
`a woman with only a pension that does not qualify` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion`
        (LIST `income of kind` `a pension paid by a former employer` `of` 20000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
        `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` `a woman with only a pension that does not qualify` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING)

-- The claim is an election: with the entitlement but no claim, no separate calculation is made.
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)  `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING)

§ `Tests — section 66(a)(2), the income not from personal exertion`

GIVEN `registered salary` IS A NUMBER
      `other salary`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`spouses in 2025 earning` `registered salary` `and` `other salary` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` `registered salary` `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` `other salary`      `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING

-- "בן הזוג שהכנסתו החייבת מיגיעה אישית גבוהה יותר", both ways.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 120000) EQUALS `registered spouse`
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 300000) EQUALS `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
-- One shekel either side of equal.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 199999) EQUALS `registered spouse`
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 200001) EQUALS `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
-- "לא היתה לבני הזוג הכנסה חייבת מיגיעה אישית": the registered spouse.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 0 `and` 0) EQUALS `registered spouse`
-- Equal and not nil: neither sentence answers (fork F3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 200000)
        BECAUSE "s 66(a)(2) does not say which spouse takes the income not from personal exertion where their incomes from personal exertion are equal"
-- Fork F4: the comparison takes the whole income from personal exertion,
-- including a pension that may not be calculated separately.  The woman has
-- 60,000 + 20,000 = 80,000 against the man's 70,000, so she is "higher".
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 70000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` `a woman with a salary and a pension that does not qualify` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING) EQUALS `spouse who is not the registered spouse`

§ `Tests — section 66(a)(3), the income of a child under 18`

GIVEN `kids` IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`spouses in 2025 with children` `kids` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` `kids` `; common source` NOTHING

-- Born 2015: turns 10 in 2025.  Born 2008: turns 17.  Born 2007: turns 18 in
-- 2025, so has "turned 18 in the tax year" and is outside (a)(3).  Born 2026:
-- not yet born in 2025.
`the registered spouse's child turning 10, interest 4000` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2015 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` FALSE `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 4000
`the registered spouse's child turning 17, interest 1000` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2008 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE  `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 1000
`the registered spouse's child turning 18, interest 3000` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2007 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE  `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 3000
`the other spouse's child alone, turning 10, interest 2000` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2015 `; of the registered spouse` FALSE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 2000
`a child born after the tax year, interest 500` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2026 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE  `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 500

#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` EMPTY) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `the registered spouse's child turning 10, interest 4000`
#ASSERT     `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` EMPTY) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `the registered spouse's child turning 17, interest 1000`
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` EMPTY) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `the registered spouse's child turning 18, interest 3000`
-- Fork F5: "ילדו" is the registered spouse's child.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` EMPTY) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `the other spouse's child alone, turning 10, interest 2000`
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` EMPTY) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `a child born after the tax year, interest 500`
-- 4000 + 1000; the other three contribute nothing.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`spouses in 2025 with children` (LIST `the registered spouse's child turning 10, interest 4000`, `the registered spouse's child turning 17, interest 1000`, `the registered spouse's child turning 18, interest 3000`, `the other spouse's child alone, turning 10, interest 2000`, `a child born after the tax year, interest 500`)) EQUALS 5000
-- The four sources (a)(3) names are added together: 100 + 200 + 300 + 400.
`a child with income from all four sources` MEANS
    `A child, for section 66` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                              IS 2015
        `a child of the registered spouse`               IS TRUE
        `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS TRUE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `taxable income from a transparent company`      IS 100
        `taxable income from a real estate investment trust` IS 200
        `taxable income from interest`                   IS 300
        `taxable income from capital gain`               IS 400
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the income within the paragraph, of` `a child with income from all four sources` EQUALS 1000

§ `Tests — section 66(b), property income`

-- The man (registered) has 30,000 from property he owned a year before the
-- marriage; the woman 40,000 from property inherited during it.  Both claim
-- under (b).  The woman also claims under (a)(1).
`a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a man` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 200000) `; other income` 10000
        `; pre-marriage property income` 30000 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; claims under (b)` TRUE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE
`a woman with inherited property, claiming (a) and (b)` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion`
        (LIST `a salary of` 120000, `income of kind` `a pension paid by a former employer` `of` 20000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` FALSE `; qualified in the five years before:` FALSE)
        `; other income` 5000 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 40000
        `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` TRUE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE
`a woman with inherited property, claiming (b) only` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 120000) `; other income` 5000
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 40000
        `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; claims under (b)` TRUE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE
`a woman with inherited property, not claiming (b)` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 120000) `; other income` 5000
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 40000
        `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

`the property couple` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` `a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` `; other` `a woman with inherited property, claiming (a) and (b)`
        `; children` (LIST `the registered spouse's child turning 10, interest 4000`, `the registered spouse's child turning 18, interest 3000`) `; common source` NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 66(b) — the property income of` `a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` EQUALS 30000
-- The proviso: the woman has an (a)(1) separate calculation, so her (b)
-- income joins it.
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — for` `the property couple` `, the property income goes:` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` EQUALS `it is added to the spouse's other income for which a separate calculation is made`
-- Fork F7: the registered spouse has no "other income for which a separate
-- calculation is made", so his is calculated on its own.
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — for` `the property couple` `, the property income goes:` `registered spouse` EQUALS `it is calculated separately on its own`
-- Without an (a)(1) calculation the woman's (b) income stands alone.
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` `a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` `; other` `a woman with inherited property, claiming (b) only` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING) `, the property income goes:` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` EQUALS `it is calculated separately on its own`
-- No claim, no separate calculation.
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` `a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` `; other` `a woman with inherited property, not claiming (b)` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING) `, the property income goes:` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` EQUALS `it is not calculated separately`
-- A claim with no such income is no claim: "בן זוג שהיתה לו הכנסה מרכוש ...".
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(b) — may claim a separate calculation of the property income:` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)

§ `Tests — sections 66(a) and (b) together`

-- S1.  Man (registered) salary 200,000 and other income 10,000; woman salary
-- 120,000 and other income 5,000, claiming (a).  (a)(2): 200,000 > 120,000,
-- so the pooled 15,000 goes to the man.  Registered: 200,000 + 15,000 =
-- 215,000.  Separate: 120,000.  No (b) income.
`S1` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a spouse:` `a man`   `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 200000) `; other income` 10000 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 120000) `; other income` 5000  `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` TRUE  `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE)
        `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` `S1` EQUALS `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` 215000 120000 0

-- S2.  As S1 but the woman earns 300,000: the pool goes to her.
-- Registered 200,000; separate 300,000 + 15,000 = 315,000.
`S2` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a spouse:` `a man`   `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 200000) `; other income` 10000 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 300000) `; other income` 5000  `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` TRUE  `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE)
        `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` `S2` EQUALS `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` 200000 315000 0

-- S3.  Equal incomes from personal exertion: the whole answer is refused (fork F3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`spouses in 2025 earning` 200000 `and` 200000)
        BECAUSE "s 66(a)(2) does not say which spouse takes the income not from personal exertion where their incomes from personal exertion are equal"

-- S4.  No claim under (a), no (b) income: s 65 governs, nothing carved out.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING) EQUALS `subsection (a) does not apply, and section 65 governs save for subsection (b)` 0 0

-- S5.  A common source failing (d), so no (a) calculation; the woman's (b)
-- claim stands "notwithstanding (a) and s 65" and, with no other separate
-- calculation, alone: 40,000.  The man's 30,000 alone too.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` `a man with pre-marriage property, claiming (b)` `; other` `a woman with inherited property, claiming (a) and (b)` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` `a common source failing (a)`) EQUALS `subsection (a) does not apply, and section 65 governs save for subsection (b)` 30000 40000

-- S6.  `the property couple`.  Man: salary 200,000; other income 10,000;
-- pre-marriage property 30,000 claimed under (b).  Woman: salary 120,000;
-- former employer's pension 20,000 meeting neither condition; other income
-- 5,000; inherited property 40,000 claimed under (b); claims (a).  Children:
-- the man's child turning 10 with interest 4,000 (in (a)(3)); a child of both
-- turning 18 with interest 3,000 (outside (a)(3)).
--   pool (a)(2): 10,000 + 5,000, no unclaimed (b) income      = 15,000
--   (a)(2): man 200,000 > woman 120,000 + 20,000 = 140,000   -> man
--   registered: 200,000 + 20,000 (her pension, kept out by the proviso)
--               + 4,000 ((a)(3)) + 15,000 (pool)              = 239,000
--   separate:   120,000 + 40,000 ((b) proviso)                = 160,000
--   the man's (b) income on its own (fork F7)                 =  30,000
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` `the property couple` EQUALS `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` 239000 160000 30000

-- S7.  As S1 but the woman does not claim (b) on 40,000 of inherited property
-- income: it is pooled.  Pool 10,000 + 5,000 + 40,000 = 55,000 -> man.
-- Registered 200,000 + 55,000 = 255,000; separate 120,000.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2025 `; registered` (`a spouse:` `a man` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` 200000) `; other income` 10000 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE) `; other` `a woman with inherited property, not claiming (b)` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING) EQUALS `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` 255000 120000 0

-- S8.  Tax year 2023: the deposited text does not govern it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`spouses in tax year` 2023 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE) `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING)
        BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"
-- 2024, the first year it governs, answers.
