§ `Tests — the tax years, rule by rule (version 0.2.0, 02-V4)`

-- Assumption A1 (ito66-tax-years.l4): the deposited text governs tax years
-- from 2024, and every rule that takes the couple refuses an earlier year.
-- Before 0.2.0 only three rules did; the independent tests found seven more
-- answering 2023 (V-4).  Each rule that takes the couple is asked of 2023 and
-- of 2024, with the same facts: a salaried registered man (200,000, not
-- claiming) and a salaried woman (120,000) claiming under (a)(1); one child of
-- both, born 2015, with interest of 4,000; no common source.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`the year-gate couple in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` `the year`
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` (LIST `the year-gate child`) `; common source` NOTHING
`the year-gate child` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2015 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 4000

