-- (4A): the child is her own, not only her husband's.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(c)(4A), (6) — a child of the widowed partner of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the year-gate couple in tax year` 2024) `:` `the year-gate child`
-- (c)(4)(a): a child turning 9, "החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים": 2.
#ASSERT     `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the year-gate couple in tax year` 2024) `for` `the year-gate child` EQUALS 2

§ `Tests — the half point under section 36A and section 48A (version 0.2.0, 02-R2)`

-- s 66(c)(4) gives the woman half a point "לפי סעיף 36א"; s 48A (line 1811)
-- may take Chapter Three's credits from a foreign worker and is not encoded.
-- Row IL-01 declines s 36A for a woman who is a foreign worker, and this row
-- now declines the half point in the same words (assumed, not ruled: the
-- lead's choice).  The children's points, s 66's own, still answer.
GIVEN `the sex`        IS A `Sex`
      `salary`         IS A NUMBER
      `claims`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`a salaried spouse:` `the sex` `earning` `salary` `; claims under (a)` `claims` `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `foreign worker` MEANS
    `a spouse, with the foreign-worker fact:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` `salary`) `; other income` 0
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` `claims` `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE
        `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `foreign worker`

GIVEN `the man is one`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman is one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` `the man is one` `; the woman a foreign worker:` `the woman is one` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2025
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `the man is one`)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE  `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `the woman is one`)
        `; children` (LIST `a child of both, born in tax year` 2015) `; common source` NOTHING

-- Reads the record (c) gives, for the tests; not a rule of law.
GIVEN w IS A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 66(c)`
`the credit points in` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in a separate calculation` cp THEN cp
    WHEN `section 66(c) does not govern the spouse's calculation` THEN REFUSE "the test expected a separate calculation"

`what (c) gives the foreign-worker woman` MEANS
    `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in`
        (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` FALSE `; the woman a foreign worker:` TRUE)

-- The half point alone, by spouse.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; a foreign worker within section 48A` TRUE)
        BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; a foreign worker within section 48A` FALSE) EQUALS 0.5
-- A man: s 36A does not reach him, so s 48A cannot change the answer (IL-01 alike).
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE `; a foreign worker within section 48A` TRUE) EQUALS 0

-- The woman a foreign worker, the man not; their child turns 2025 - 2015 = 10.
-- Her half point under s 36A: declined.  Her children's points, (c)(4)(a)
-- "ושתי נקודות זיכוי ... החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים": 2.  s 37: none.
-- Asked as a whole, the record refuses, because it holds the declined half point.
#ASSERT REFUSED `what (c) gives the foreign-worker woman`
        BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the credit points in` `what (c) gives the foreign-worker woman`)'s `one half point under section 36A, by paragraph (4)`
        BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT (`the credit points in` `what (c) gives the foreign-worker woman`)'s `points for children, by paragraphs (4), (4A), (5) and (6)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`the credit points in` `what (c) gives the foreign-worker woman`)'s `one half point under section 37, by paragraph (2)` EQUALS 0
-- The same, provision by provision: s 36A declined; s 34 still "each of the
-- spouses" under (c)(1) (whether s 34 gives her points is IL-01's count).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` FALSE `; the woman a foreign worker:` TRUE) `has the entitlement under` `section 36A`
        BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` FALSE `; the woman a foreign worker:` TRUE) `has the entitlement under` `section 34`

-- The man a foreign worker, the woman not.  He has no half point to lose:
-- 0, 0, and (c)(5)(c) "נקודת זיכוי אחת ... החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים": 1.
-- She keeps her half point and 2 for the child.
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in` (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` TRUE `; the woman a foreign worker:` FALSE) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0 0 1)
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` TRUE `; the woman a foreign worker:` FALSE) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0.5 0 2)
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, the` `registered spouse` `in` (`the 48A couple in 2025; the man a foreign worker:` TRUE `; the woman a foreign worker:` FALSE) `has the entitlement under` `section 36A`

§ `Tests — fork F19, an election for a child born before 2024 (version 0.3.0, SHRUG)`

-- Ruled by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default DECLINE.
-- (c)(4)(a1), line 2467: the mother may have one point "מתוך נקודות הזיכוי
-- שלהן היא זכאית כאמור באותה פסקה, בשנת הלידה" counted in the following tax
-- year.  For a child born in 2023 the year of birth is governed by a text
-- this row does not hold (A1), so by default a 2024 calculation that would
-- carry the point is declined.  Reading (i), the behaviour of 0.1.0-0.2.0,
-- is kept by name: (c)(4)(a), line 2466, gives 4½ "החל בשנת המס שלאחר שנת
-- לידתו", and the point moved makes 4½ + 1 = 5½.
`a child born 2023, the mother deferring` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2023 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` TRUE `; interest` 0

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`the F19 couple in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` `the year`
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` (LIST `a child born 2023, the mother deferring`) `; common source` NOTHING

-- The switch.
#ASSERT `section 66(c)(4)(a1) — the reading this row takes for an election for a child born before 2024` EQUALS `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`

-- The mother's points in 2024: declined by default and by name; 5½ under (i).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `in tax year` 2024
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `in tax year` 2024 `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `in tax year` 2024 `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation` EQUALS 5.5
-- Under either reading the year gate comes first: 2023 itself is A1's refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `in tax year` 2023 `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation`
        BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"

-- Where the fork is not reached, the default answers.
-- No election: 4½ for a child turning 1 (line 2466).
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` (`a child of both, born in tax year` 2023) `in tax year` 2024 EQUALS 4.5
-- The election moves nothing out of the year after birth: turning 2 in 2025, 4½.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 4.5
-- A child born in 2024, a year the text governs: 4½ + 1 = 5½ in 2025 (line 2467).
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` (`a child born in tax year` 2024 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` TRUE `; interest` 0) `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 5.5

-- One child, for the woman, through (c)(4)-(6).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024) `for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024) `for` `a child born 2023, the mother deferring` `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation` EQUALS 5.5

-- The whole of (c) for the couple in 2024.  The woman: declined by default
-- and by name; under (i), ½ (s 36A, line 2465), no s 37 point, 5½.  The man:
-- the election is the mother's ("אמו של ילד"), so (c)(5)(b), line 2475, gives
-- him 4½ "החל בשנת המס שלאחר לידתו" under the default too.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024)
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024) `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024) `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation` EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0.5 0 5.5)
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in` (`the F19 couple in tax year` 2024) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0 0 4.5)
